## Tutorials

❮ Java Keywords

Thecatchkeyword catches exceptions generated bytrystatements.

The catch statement allows you to define a block of code to be executed, if an error occurs in the try block.

Read more about exceptions in ourJava Try..Catch Tutorial.

❮ Java Keywords

### Code Examples

```
Example
If an error occur, use try...catch to catch the error and execute some code to handle it:
try {
  int[] myNumbers = {1, 2, 3};
  System.out.println(myNumbers[10]);
} catch (Exception e) {
  System.out.println("Something went wrong.");
}
Try it Yourself »
```

